Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0
Recommends: fonts-noto-color-emoji, libxtst6
Suggests: tesseract-ocr
Description: clipboard history and emoji panel with Windows-style shortcuts
 SuperV brings the Windows clipboard history (Win+V) and emoji panel (Win+.)
 to the Linux desktop. Super+V shows the last 25 copied items, text and
 images; clicking one pastes it into the application in use. Items can be
 pinned, and unpinned history is cleared on reboot.
 .
 Optional extras, off until turned on in its settings: an emoji panel
 (Super+.), plain-text paste, a colour picker, copying text from the screen
 (with tesseract-ocr) and an annotating screenshot tool.
 .
 It works on GNOME, Cinnamon, MATE and Xfce, on Wayland and X11, and never
 uses the network.
